THE GRACE INTERMEDIATE FIELD MODEL GIF48
=============================================

Contact: 
John C. Ries 
email: ries@csr.utexas.edu

Reference:
----------
Mean Background Gravity Fields for GRACE Processing, GRACE Science Team Meeting, 
Austin, TX, 8-10 August 2011  (J. C. Ries, S. Bettadpur, S. Poole, and T. Richter).

ftp://ftp.csr.utexas.edu/pub/grace/GIF48/GSTM2011_Ries_etal.pdf

In preparation for Release 5 reprocessing of the GRACE mission at UT/CSR, an improved
mean gravity field has been prepared. GIF48 is an 'informal' combination of GRACE
and terrestrial gravity information, complete to degree and order 360. 
GIF48 was determined from a selection of 66 months spanning 2003 through 2010.
Not all months were used; months where the groundtrack was in a deep repeat were
excluded, since these seemed to slightly degrade the overall solution quality.
The terrestrial gravity information was taken from the DTU10 global gravity field.
The combination used variance information only rather a full variance/covariance
solution. Information regarding DUT10 is available at:

http://www.space.dtu.dk/English/Research/Scientific_data_and_models/Global_Marine_Gravity_Field.aspx

Please note: the reference epoch of this gravity field model is 1 January 2007. Any 
terms with rates in the background modeling have been mapped to this epoch. In addition,
a correction for the change in the mean field due to the Sumatra-Andaman earthquake has been
applied to the months that followed that event. For additional details on the background 
modeling, see the CSR RL04 processing standards document available at:

ftp://podaac.jpl.nasa.gov/pub/grace/doc/L2-CSR0004_ProcStd_v3.1.pdf


